 parts.","image":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 130 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" font-family=\"JetBrains Mono, monospace\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"55\"/><line x1=\"65\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"65\" y2=\"10\"/><line x1=\"65\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"65\"/><line x1=\"65\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"105\"/><text x=\"78\" y=\"55\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">¼</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"92\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"92\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x</text></svg>","topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the shaded area in the given rectangle (a triangle inside a rectangle; bottom split \\( 8 \\) and \\( 4 \\), right split \\( 2 \\) and \\( 6 \\)).","options":["\\( 40 \\)","\\( 50 \\)","\\( 54 \\)","\\( 68 \\)","\\( 90 \\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["With the given splits the shaded triangle works out to \\( 54 \\). ⚠ Strongly figure-dependent — verify against the official key."],"hint":"Find the rectangle's dimensions, then use \\( \\tfrac{1}{2}\\,b\\,h \\) for the triangle.","image":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 200 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" font-family=\"JetBrains Mono, monospace\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"15\" width=\"160\" height=\"100\"/><path d=\"M20 15 L180 55 L100 115 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-opacity=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"128\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"128\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"35\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"11\" 