ge":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the odd one out: \\( 3, 5, 11, 14, 17, 21 \\).","options":["\\( 3 \\)","\\( 5 \\)","\\( 11 \\)","\\( 14 \\)","\\( 21 \\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\( 14 \\) is the only even number; the rest are odd."],"hint":"Look at which is even.","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the odd one out: \\( 6, 9, 15, 21, 24, 28, 30 \\).","options":["\\( 6 \\)","\\( 9 \\)","\\( 15 \\)","\\( 21 \\)","\\( 28 \\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\( 28 \\) is not a multiple of \\( 3 \\); all the others are."],"hint":"Which is not a multiple of \\( 3 \\)?","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the odd one out: \\( 396, 462, 572, 427, 671, 264 \\).","options":["\\( 396 \\)","\\( 462 \\)","\\( 427 \\)","\\( 671 \\)","\\( 264 \\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\( 396,462,572,671,264 \\) are all divisible by \\( 11 \\); \\( 427 \\) is not."],"hint":"Test each for divisibility by \\( 11 \\).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the wrong number in the series: \\( 1, 1, 2, 6, 24, 96, 720 \\).","options":["\\( 2 \\)","\\( 6 \\)","\\( 24 \\)","\\( 96 \\)","\\( 720 \\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\( 5! = 120 \\), not \\( 96 \\); so \\( 96 \\) is wrong."],"hint":"These should be the factorials \\( 0!,1!,2!,3!,4!,5!,6! \\).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"\\( 12593 \\) is to \\( 35291 \\) and \\( 29684 \\) is to \\( 46982 \\). Therefore \\( 72936 \\) is to ?","options":["\\( 69237 \\)","\\( 69732 \\)","\\( 67329 \\)","\\( 39267 \\)","\\( 36297 \\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Positions map \\( (1,2,3,4,5)\\to(5,3,2,4,1) \\): \\( 72936 \\to 69237 \\)."],"hint":"The digits are rearranged by a fixed position pattern (the middle digit stays put).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"In each triangle a number sits in the middle. Triangles: \\( (4 \\text{ top}, 7, 9 \\to 12) \\), \\( (1,1,4 \\to 4) \\), \\( (2,6,5 \\to ?) \\). Which number replaces the question mark?","options":["\\( 7 \\)","\\( 9 \\)","\\( 12 \\)","\\( 14 \\)","\\( 18 \\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\( 7+9-4=12 \\), \\( 1+4-1=4 \\), so \\( 6+5-2 = 9 \\)."],"hint":"Middle \\( = \\) (bottom-left) \\( + \\) (bottom-right) \\( - \\) (top).","image":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 110\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" font-family=\"JetBrains Mono, monospace\"><path d=\"M40 20 L70 90 L10 90 Z\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"30\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"75\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"86\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">7</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"86\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><path d=\"M120 20 L150 90 L90 90 Z\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"30\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"75\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"86\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"86\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><path d=\"M200 20 L230 90 L170 90 Z\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"75\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"